The O3DE lighting investigation's picks
=======================================

A click on the scene, or on a view of a screen-sized resource (a forward target, the depth, the stencil), picks
the pixel there: the surface point the readout inspects, which every such view rings where it projects
(`pickShown`). The lab traces the ray (`trace`); this says what the hit sets.

$[Import* std]
$[Import* render_lab_runtime]
$[Import* o3de_lighting_values]
$[Import* o3de_lighting_natives]
$[ImportAs rl_runtime rt]

The values a hit sets: the point, its normal turned to face the viewer, and the object. Nothing when the ray
misses (the ceiling's light panel is not a surface the readout inspects).
$[# {_pick click} {caseOption
    {rt::trace {.u click} {.v click} {' "emissive panel"}}
    {^ {} {'}}
    {^ {hit}
        [# n {!if {> {vdot {.normal hit} {.dir hit}} 0.0}
            {vscale {.normal hit} -1.0}
            {.normal hit}}]
        [# p {.point hit}]
        {'
            {setPickShown 1.0}
            {setInspectX {.x p}}
            {setInspectY {.y p}}
            {setInspectZ {.z p}}
            {setInspectNX {.x n}}
            {setInspectNY {.y n}}
            {setInspectNZ {.z n}}
            {setInspectObject {float {.object hit}}}}}}]

Picks the pixel clicked on a view of a screen-sized resource: ringed in every such view, and its surface point
inspected in the scene.
$[# pickPixel {: _pick ClickHandler}]

Picks the pixel of the inspected tile under a click on the zoomed tile view (`tilePixels`): the click's cell
becomes its pixel on the viewport, which is picked as a click there would be.
$[# pickTilePixel {: {^ {click}
    [# at {tileCell {.u click} {.v click}}]
    {_pick {: {. u {.u at} v {.v at}} Click}}} ClickHandler}]

Picks the entry of the tile's list under a click on the list view (`lightList`, 960 x 420, 32 columns after a
16-pixel margin, 11 rows): its first two rows hold the tile's list, so only they pick.
$[# pickListSlot {: {^ {click}
    [# x {- {* {.u click} 960.0} 16.0}]
    [# col {float {floor {/ x {/ 944.0 32.0}}}}]
    [# row {float {floor {* {.v click} 11.0}}}]
    {!if {!and {>= x 0.0} {< row 2.0}} {' {setListPick {+ {* row 32.0} col}}} {'}}} ClickHandler}]

A click on the back wall where the illustrated atlas hangs picks the map there (-1 elsewhere).
$[# {_atlasPick click} {caseOption
    {rt::trace {.u click} {.v click} {' "emissive panel"}}
    {^ {} {'}}
    {^ {hit} {!if {!and {> {atlasMaps} 0.0} {= {.object hit} 1}}
        {' {setAtlasPick {atlasMapAt {.x {.point hit}} {.y {.point hit}}}}}
        {'}}}}]

A click on the scene picks its pixel and inspects its point, and a map of the illustrated atlas when it lands on
one.
$[# scene {: {^ {click} {append {_pick click} {_atlasPick click}}} ClickHandler}]
